A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate when it **shares a cause** with an open ticket
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause), which replaces
[0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)):

1. look up the reporter's tenant: its locale and booking form;
2. work out the cause from them, ignoring the subject and intake's tag;
3. found an open ticket with that cause: merge. None: open a new ticket.

<Callout>
Matching on subject hid two causes inside #4471. Match on cause.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Look up the tenant. A wrong merge hides a second bug behind a fix that does not cover it.
